      "writtenOn": "2023-05-23T20:32:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It turns out that `IS_ENABLED` only works for config macros (i.e. `CONFIG_*`). Testing this out on a normal macro results in a link error like this:\n\n```\nld.lld: error: undefined symbol: IS_ENABLED_BAD_ARGS\n\u003e\u003e\u003e referenced by fpc_private.c:372 (/mnt/host/source/src/platform/ec/driver/fingerprint/fpc/libfp/fpc_private.c:372)\n```\n\nOne alternative strategy would be to add a field to the driver to represent whether we have a private repo. Something like:\n```\n\n#ifdef HAVE_PRIVATE\n#define FP_SENSOR_DRIVER_HAS_PRIVATE (true)\n#else\n#define FP_SENSOR_DRIVER_HAS_PRIVATE (false)\n#endif\n\nstruct fp_sensor_interface {\n\tconst enum fp_sensor_type sensor_type;\n        const bool has_private \u003d FP_SENSOR_DRIVER_HAS_PRIVATE;\n...\n```\n\nOtherwise we could leave it as-is or devise a more generic strategy similar to `IS_ENABLED` (although I\u0027m not sure how that would be done)",
